<h2>Uploading Documents</h2>
<h3>Step-by-Step</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Open the case</strong> you\'re uploading to</li>
<li><strong>Navigate to the Documents section</strong></li>
<li><strong>Click "Upload Document"</strong></li>
<li><strong>Select the document type</strong> from the dropdown (income verification, before photo, etc.)</li>
<li><strong>Choose the file</strong> from your device<ul>
<li>Accepted formats: PDF, JPG, PNG</li>
<li>Max file size: 25MB per file</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Add a description</strong> (optional but helpful) — "Before - Roof, east section"</li>
<li><strong>Upload</strong></li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Name your files before uploading. "before_roof_east.jpg" is infinitely more useful than "IMG_4721.jpg."</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Uploading Multiple Files at Once</h3>
<p>The platform supports multi-file upload. Select all the files you want to upload at once, and the system will process them as a batch.</p>
<p><strong>Best practice:</strong> Upload files of the same type together. Don\'t mix before photos with invoices — upload them as separate batches with appropriate document types.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Photo Best Practices</h2>
<h3>Before Photos</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wide shot</strong> showing the full repair area</li>
<li><strong>Close-up</strong> showing the specific damage</li>
<li><strong>Include a reference</strong> for scale (hand, ruler, coin)</li>
<li><strong>Same angles</strong> you\'ll use for after photos</li>
<li><strong>Label with room/area</strong> — "Kitchen ceiling, northwest corner"</li>
</ul>
<h3>After Photos</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Same angles</strong> as before photos (side-by-side comparison is powerful)</li>
<li><strong>Well-lit</strong> — turn on lights, open blinds, use flash</li>
<li><strong>Clean workspace</strong> — no tools, debris, or ladders in the shot</li>
<li><strong>Label clearly</strong> — "After - Roof repair, east section, 9/15/2026"</li>
</ul>
<h3>During Photos</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Progress milestones</strong> — demo complete, rough-in installed, drywall hung</li>
<li><strong>Hidden work</strong> — things that will be covered up (wiring behind walls, subfloor under finish floor)</li>
<li><strong>Unexpected findings</strong> — "Opened wall, found mold on insulation"</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Grant reporting gold:</strong> Before/after side-by-side comparisons are the single most compelling evidence for funders. Take the time to get them right.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Finding Documents</h2>
<h3>In a Case</h3>
<p>Open the case and go to the Documents tab. You can:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Filter by type</strong> — show only photos, only invoices, etc.</li>
<li><strong>Sort by date</strong> — newest first, or oldest first</li>
<li><strong>Search by description</strong> — if someone labeled files well</li>
</ul>
<h3>Across Cases</h3>
<p>Use Case Search with document filters to find:</p>
<ul>
<li>All cases with missing after photos</li>
<li>All cases with uploaded contracts</li>
<li>All cases from a specific date range with documents</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Document Security</h2>
<h3>Who Can See What</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Document Type</th>
<th>Visible To</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Income verification</td>
<td>Assigned caseworker, Admin, Bursar</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Photo ID</td>
<td>Assigned caseworker, Admin</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Photos (before/during/after)</td>
<td>All assigned staff, applicant</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Contracts</td>
<td>PM, Admin, applicant</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Invoices</td>
<td>Bursar, PM, Admin</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Assessments</td>
<td>All assigned staff</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Sensitive documents</strong> (income verification, ID) have restricted access. Only people who need them for eligibility determination can view them.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>What Applicants Can See</h3>
<p>Applicants can see:</p>
<ul>
<li>Photos of their own property</li>
<li>Contracts they\'ve signed</li>
<li>Communication logs addressed to them</li>
</ul>
<p>Applicants <strong>cannot</strong> see:</p>
<ul>
<li>Other applicants\' documents</li>
<li>Internal staff notes</li>
<li>Financial records (invoices, payment records)</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Common Problems &amp; Solutions</h2>
<h3>"My Upload Keeps Failing"</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Check file size</strong> — is it over 25MB? Compress it or split it</li>
<li><strong>Check file type</strong> — is it a PDF, JPG, or PNG? Other formats aren\'t accepted</li>
<li><strong>Check your connection</strong> — a slow internet connection can timeout large uploads</li>
<li><strong>Try a different browser</strong> — some browsers handle large uploads better</li>
</ul>
<h3>"A Photo Disappeared"</h3>
<ul>
<li>Check the <strong>trash/version history</strong> — deleted files may be recoverable</li>
<li>Check if someone <strong>re-categorized</strong> it — it may be under a different document type</li>
<li>Check the <strong>activity log</strong> — who uploaded it, and was it later deleted?</li>
</ul>
<h3>"I Can\'t See a Document I Know Exists"</h3>
<ul>
<li>Check your <strong>permissions</strong> — some documents are restricted to certain roles</li>
<li>Check the <strong>case</strong> — are you looking at the right case?</li>
<li>Ask the <strong>caseworker</strong> — they can see what documents are attached and who can view them</li>
</ul>
<hr />
